><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20250523105131+10'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20250523105146+10'00'" name="21b107d1-0719-4f7f-a98c-619f4db9b541" page="10" coords="509.155000,240.626000,568.520000,240.626000,509.155000,229.467000,568.520000,229.467000,316.500000,229.524000,568.517000,229.524000,316.500000,218.365000,568.517000,218.365000,316.500000,218.422000,568.538000,218.422000,316.500000,207.263000,568.538000,207.263000,316.500000,207.320000,568.525000,207.320000,316.500000,196.161000,568.525000,196.161000,316.500000,196.218000,568.541000,196.218000,316.500000,185.059000,568.541000,185.059000,316.500000,185.116000,568.525000,185.116000,316.500000,173.957000,568.525000,173.957000,316.500000,174.014000,568.513000,174.014000,316.500000,162.855000,568.513000,162.855000,316.500000,162.912000,568.519000,162.912000,316.500000,151.753000,568.519000,151.753000,316.500000,151.810000,568.521000,151.810000,316.500000,140.651000,568.521000,140.651000,316.500000,140.708000,568.540000,140.708000,316.500000,129.549000,568.540000,129.549000,316.500000,129.606000,568.514000,129.606000,316.500000,118.447000,568.514000,118.447000,316.500000,118.504000,568.523000,118.504000,316.500000,107.345000,568.523000,107.345000,316.500000,107.402000,568.518000,107.402000,316.500000,96.242500,568.518000,96.242500,316.500000,96.300400,568.520000,96.300400,316.500000,85.140500,568.520000,85.140500,316.500000,85.198400,568.530000,85.198400,316.500000,74.038500,568.530000,74.038500,316.500000,74.096400,568.510000,74.096400,316.500000,62.936500,568.510000,62.936500,316.500000,62.994400,568.506000,62.994400,316.500000,51.834500,568.506000,51.834500" rect="316.151000,51.485800,568.890000,240.975000" subject="Comment on Text" title="alexd"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
> It is also&#xD;recommended in future studies to verify ROI selection with a&#xD;second assessor, as previously seen when tracing muscle&#xD;boundaries to calculate CSA in cervical musculature (36).&#xD;Verification of ROI selection by a second assessor was not&#xD;mentioned in any of the studies included in this review.&#xD;Appropriate ROI selection is an important factor for T2 relaxometry&#xD;value calculation, as different values are characteristic&#xD;of different tissues (29). Therefore, the accidental inclusion of&#xD;fat, blood vessels, aponeurosis, bone, and tendon in a ROI will&#xD;affect T2 relaxometry values. ROI selection should be verified&#xD;by a second assessor and reliability of ROI selection reported.&#xD;Lastly, to capture peak T2 relaxometry values, the time between&#xD;exercise cessation and scan acquisition completion&#xD;should be kept to a minimum by adjusting MRI scan acquisition&#xD;time and exercise protocol type and location. Considerations&#xD;should also be made regarding the number of TE </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>included within the scanning parameters, as this affects both&#xD;scan acquisition time and T2 relaxation value calculations.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="10" rect="612.000000,148.626000,796.000000,240.626000"
/></highlight
